       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g/day, and many hospitals cap it at 3 g/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This could cause hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2600 mg/day)\n\nTell me which you want, or confirm that you really want 2000 mg three times daily and I'll enter it with a note. Include any other acetaminophen sources the patient is getting, such as combination products or IV doses, so the total stays within limits."
